</think>The integral  

\[
\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{1+t^{2}}\,dt
\]

is a standard one.  

It is the integral of the arctangent function from \(0\) to \(\infty\):

\[
\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{1+t^{2}}\,dt = \arctan t \Big|_{0}^{\infty}.
\]

When the upper limit is \(\infty\), \(\arctan(\infty) = \frac{\pi}{2}\).  
Thus the integral equals  

\[
\frac{\pi}{2}.
\]

\[
\boxed{\frac{\pi}{2}}
\]

